tBHarpL = { cis,4\pp r4 r4 | cis,4 r4 r4 | fis,,4 r4 r4 | gis,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,4 r4 r4 | fis,,4 r4 r4 | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }
tBVlnOne = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | fis''2(\p\< gis''4 | a''2 cis'''4) | b''4.( a''8 gis''4~ | gis''4 fis''2) | e'''4(\f fis'''8 e'''8 dis'''8 e'''8 | cis'''4 gis''2) | a''2( b''8 cis'''8) | gis''2.\> | a'4--\p r4 r4 | c''4-- r4 r4 | b'4-- r4 r4 | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | }  % c070: 203 the top voice's flat 6 (C5, A minor at 202) falls to 5 (B4) over the B pedal in its own register, with Bsn 1 and Hn 4 an octave lower (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 23, PDF 388 and PDF 401 point 3: once introduced, flat 6 moves to 5)
% c107: 197-200 Vln II plays the trio tune's head with the violas (unison G sharp 4-E5) instead of the call's lower octave, which crossed the violas' tune in the same colour
%   and register and met it in rhythm at 199-200 (Adler I PDF 144 rules 3-4: theme and countertheme apart in register and rhythm; PDF 135: background out of the melody's register in like colour).
%   The call keeps Fl 1-2 and Vln I at E6 and Ob 1 at E5.
% s125 (cycle 125): 201-202 Vln II tenutos above: under C sharp 4/E4 they sat where a ledger line goes and the one at 201 touched the p (Gould PDF 55-56)
