% c177: 201-203 violas hold the top line A4-C5-B4 (the flat 6-5 of c070) under Vln I's tenuto crotchets, instead of a fourth E4 (with Cl 2, Hn 3 and Vln II) and a third D sharp 4 (Adler I PDF 257: unison overlapping only gives a stronger pitch; PDF 255: the line must come through the harmony; PDF 270, Copland: the weak line gets the doubling). Bar 204 F sharp 4 unchanged.
tBVla = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | a4(\p\<^\markup \italic "unis." b8 a gis a) | a2. | b4( cis'8 b ais b) | b2. | gis'2(\f_\markup \italic "espress." a'4 | b'2 e''4) | dis''4.( cis''8 b'4) | a'4(\> gis'2) | a'2.\p | c''2. | b'2.\> | fis'2. | fis2.\pp | fis2. | fis2.\< | fis2. | }
% c102: 195 bass B, tied into 196 (was G sharp, I6 between ii7 and V7): ii7 - V6/4 - V7, the cadential 6/4 approached by intermediate harmony; Cl 2 E4 is the 4th held as a common tone and falls to D sharp 4 (Aldwell-Schachter PDF 148 rule 3, 152-153, 160).
tBVc = { R2. | R2. | R2. | R2. | dis'4(\p^\markup \italic "dolce" e'8 dis'8 cis'8 dis'8 | b2 fis4) | gis4.( a8 b4) | fis2. | fis,2.\p\< | fis,2. | b,2.~ | b,2. | cis2.\f | cis2. | fis,2. | gis,2.\> | a,2.\p | a,2. | b,2.\> | b,2. | b,2.\pp | b,2. | b,2.\< | b,2. | }  % c011: the answer at 189-192 an octave higher, on the A and D strings, in unison with the cor anglais (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 56-57)
% c158: 185 Cb pizz. pp (was p carried from 169): the harp doubles this bass at pp under Ob 1's p solo; the pizz. bass under the trio solos is pp at 153 and 341 (c099, c148; Sebesky PDF 14: the rhythm section is the tertiary level).
tBCb = { cis,4\pp r4 r4 | cis,4 r4 r4 | fis,,4 r4 r4 | gis,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | e,4 r4 r4 | R2. | fis,,2.\p\<\upbow^\markup \italic "arco" | fis,,2. | b,,2.~ | b,,2. | cis,2.\f | cis,2. | fis,,2. | gis,,2.\> | a,,2.\p | a,,2. | b,,2.\> | b,,2\upbow r4 | b,,4\pp^\markup \italic "pizz." r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | b,,4\< r4 r4 | R2. | }
% c045: 193 Vln I and II marked p at their entry after eight bars' rest (they read mp from 169); violas, cellos and basses are p here (MOLA PDF 8).
% c112: 196 Vln II F#4-A4-G#4 (7th of V7 resolves down; removes 5ths with the bass B-C#). 201 Cl 2 B#3-C#4 (leading tone resolves; doubled 3rd of VI, A-S Ex. 13-12, PDF 202-203).
